Most Frequently Asked Linux Interview Commands (Grep Focus)

Hi everyone! 👋
I'm back with one of the most common Linux interview topics — grep.
If you're preparing for DevOps, Linux admin, or support engineer roles, these commands are must-know ✅

Here are the top 9 real-world grep use cases you’ll be asked in interviews 👇

✅ 1️⃣ Find a specific word in a file
grep "error" app.log

✅ 2️⃣ Case-insensitive search
grep -i "success" app.log


✔ Matches SUCCESS, Success, success, etc.

✅ 3️⃣ Search recursively in all files and subdirectories
grep -R "timeout" /etc/

✅ 4️⃣ Display line numbers for matched results
grep -n "connection" server.log

✅ 5️⃣ Count how many times a word appears
grep -c "error" app.log

✅ 6️⃣ Show lines that do not contain the word
grep -v "info" app.log

✅ 7️⃣ Match the whole word only
grep -w "start" script.sh


✔ Avoids matching restart or starting

✅ 8️⃣ Search for multiple patterns
grep -E "error|success|timeout" app.log

✅ 9️⃣ Find a running process using grep
ps aux | grep nginx
